\paragraph{Recommended workflow.}
Practitioners should (i) collect $n_{\text{expert}} \geq 25K / P(Z_{\text{minority}})$ stratified expert labels, (ii) verify per-subgroup budget $\geq 25$ and $\max(\text{FPR}, \text{FNR}) < 0.5$, and (iii) apply EC-HTE when Proposition~\ref{prop:debiasing_hurts} flags harmful global correction; PPCI can be composed for outcome error (Appendix~\ref{sec:ppci}).
Expert budget crossover curves and the applicability frontier appear in Appendices~\ref{sec:budget} and~\ref{app:semireal}.

